Custom surface response
-----------------------
GGX, Smith, Schlick and environment importance-sampling theory is described in
Filament: https://google.github.io/filament/main/filament.html (sections 4.2, 4.4, 4.9, 5.3, 5.6 and 9.2).
Used as mathematical reference; independently implemented, no source code copied.

Enhanced sky and cloud response
------------------------------
Cloud density profiles, weather fields, remapping and multiple-octave scattering adapted from
SkyGL (MIT), copyright 2026 Ivan Vasiliev:
https://github.com/kotivas/skygl/tree/edbbb0148091bd85261dec0a2164bc026ff01a3e
The complete notice is retained in sky_clouds.wgsl. Noise generation and native
integration are independently implemented; no SkyGL noise or atmosphere source
was copied. Base/detail texture structure follows Guerrilla's 2015 presentation:
https://www.guerrilla-games.com/read/the-real-time-volumetric-cloudscapes-of-horizon-zero-dawn
Architecture references also include Hillaire's Sky Atmosphere (MIT):
https://github.com/sebh/UnrealEngineSkyAtmosphere
and Godot's shared sky/environment design:
https://godotengine.org/article/custom-sky-shaders-godot-4-0/
See docs/enhanced-sky.md for the prototype model and limits.

